{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":2355942,"ns":0,"title":"Cartesian circle","extract":"The Cartesian circle (also known as Arnauld's circle) is an example of fallacious circular reasoning attributed to French philosopher René Descartes. He argued that the existence of God is proven by reliable perception, which is itself guaranteed by God.","description":"Error in reasoning attributed to René Descartes","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}